Disable unprefixed assertion macro names by default.

Source: CarbonHeaders-18.1 (214a9ae7ab3c0c78ddb50328ca226e6313c4c782), AssertMacros.h,
after Apple's Makefile installhdrs. Scope: macOS SDK 26.5, arm64 and x86_64.

The header's own compatibility comment announces the upcoming default.
A client function named check collides with the old macro default. Retain
the documented explicit opt-in and opt-out and match the 26.5 comparison.

Evidence: .agents/skills/review-macos-c-sdk/scripts/sdk_review/headers/data/macosx26.5/tested-header-repairs.md.

--- a/usr/include/AssertMacros.h
+++ b/usr/include/AssertMacros.h
@@ -1280,8 +1280,8 @@
  */
 
 #ifndef __ASSERT_MACROS_DEFINE_VERSIONS_WITHOUT_UNDERSCORES
-	/* If we haven't set this yet, it defaults to on.  In the next release, this will default to off. */
-	#define	__ASSERT_MACROS_DEFINE_VERSIONS_WITHOUT_UNDERSCORES	1
+	/* Define the switch to 1 to enable unprefixed assertion macros. */
+	#define	__ASSERT_MACROS_DEFINE_VERSIONS_WITHOUT_UNDERSCORES	0
 #endif
 
 #if	__ASSERT_MACROS_DEFINE_VERSIONS_WITHOUT_UNDERSCORES
